@startuml HearSayCurrent
!pragma layout smetana
title HearSay - Current Runtime Architecture
actor "Browser user" as User
package "React SPA (hearsay/src)" {
  component "App / Header\nRouter + theme/toast/auth providers" as App
  component "Public pages\nLanding, Search, Random\nArtist, Album, Song\nRecent Reviews, Review details" as Public
  component "Protected pages\nProfile, My Reviews" as Protected
  component "AuthPage / AuthCallback\nLocal auth + Google PKCE" as Auth
}
component "Vite dev proxy :5173\nor frontend Nginx :8080" as Proxy
component "Express API :5174\nhearsay/server/index.js" as API
component "dbAPI.js\nNative MongoDB driver" as DBAPI
component "spotifyAPI.js\nServer-side app token" as SpotifyAPI
database "MongoDB hearsay\nusers, reviews, artists, albums, songs" as Data
database "expressSessions\nconnect-mongo" as Sessions
cloud "Spotify Web API" as Spotify
cloud "Google token / userinfo / authorization" as Google
component "schema-HearSay-*.json\napply-schemas.mjs" as Schemas
User --> App
App --> Public
App --> Protected
App --> Auth
Public --> Proxy : fetch /api
Protected --> Proxy : cookie-authenticated fetch
Auth --> Proxy : local login and code exchange
Auth --> Google : PKCE authorization redirect
Proxy --> API
API --> DBAPI
DBAPI --> Data
API --> Sessions
API --> SpotifyAPI
SpotifyAPI --> Spotify
API --> Google : code exchange + userinfo
Schemas --> Data : validators applied at container startup
note bottom of Public
 Album track submission saves individual song reviews,
 averages rated tracks, then saves an album rating.
 At least one track is required. These writes are sequential.
end note
note bottom of Auth
 AuthPage reads VITE_API_BASE at build time.
 Other pages generally use same-origin /api.
end note
@enduml
